# One/two-day coupled run used to measure OpenMP thread scaling before
# committing a multi-year campaign to a guessed OMP_NUM_THREADS.
# STA is set per-thread-count by the sibling threadscan_t*.env files.
#
# N_HOURS must make the run END AT HOUR 23 of STA's end date.
# ecland_create_namelist.py writes EHOUR=23 into the CaMa namelist (it uses
# end-of-day, not the forcing file's actual last hour), and
# ecland_run_model.sh then moves restart${EYEAR}${EMON}${EDAY}${EHOUR}.nc.
# A run ending at any other hour leaves that file non-existent and the job
# fails AFTER a successful model integration -- exit 1:0 with the model step
# itself COMPLETED. Observed 2026-09-20 with N_HOURS=25 against
# STA=..._19880101-19880102, which ends at 01:00, not 23:00.
# 1988-01-01T00 + 48h -> last hour 1988-01-02T23. Correct.
START_DATE=1988-01-01T00:00:00
N_HOURS=48
NFORCWINDOW=8
FORCING_SOURCE=${SLURM_SUBMIT_DIR}/forcing/WFDE5_CRU_GPCC/WFDE5_CRU_GPCC_1988.nc
